.TH AWKTEST 1
.SH NAME
awktest \- regression test for awk(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B awktest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Awktest
loads
.BR /p9/dis/awk.dis 's
in-process test seam,
.BR runstring(prog,\ input) ,
and checks a battery of real awk programs against golden output: field
selection, arithmetic, patterns, printf, loops,
.BR ++ / -- ,
builtins, custom
.BR FS ,
and associative-array
.RB ( for
.RI ( k " in " arr ))
enumeration.
Each expected string was checked once against
.BR utils/awk 's
real, working C implementation on the same program and input, except
the array-enumeration case, checked as a set rather than an exact
sequence since POSIX leaves that order unspecified.
.PP
Prints one line per failure to standard error, a final
.IR N " passed, " N " failed"
summary to standard output, and exits with a non-nil status if
anything failed.
.SH SOURCE
.B /p9/cmd/awktest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR awk (1)
.SH BUGS
Runs
.I awk
in-process via its
.B runstring
seam, not as a spawned subprocess reading real files and standard
input/output \(em so it does not exercise
.IR awk 's
own
.BR init ,
argument parsing, or file I/O at all. Those are exercised by hand
against
.B utils/awk/o.out
during development (see
.BR doc/plan9-port.md ),
not by this test.
